# Yardzen · Visual Identity System Redesign

Prepared for Brian Radics by Daniel Pliego, Casa Soda.

A new look for Yardzen, and everything that keeps it consistent: the brandbook, a modern cross-platform system of templates, guidelines and examples, and the handoff that lets every team member and agency apply it without us in the room.

## Why now

> "Erosion of the brand equity due to a lack of adherence to standards: inconsistent font usage, varying tones of voice, lack of brand breakthrough, and brand visuals that lack the quality standards expected."
>
> — Brand Design Brief

### Word of mouth is how Yardzen gets into high value homes

Every referral ends with someone looking Yardzen up. The website, the logo, the emails have to be as good as the design they just heard about. There's no core system making sure they are.

## Project objectives

**Elevated perception.** A premium, design-led identity that makes the promise of a premium landscape credible before anyone reads a word.

**Lifestyle brand community.** A mark with enough character that people will wear it and identify with it.

**Instill intent.** An art direction that associates Yardzen with aspiration, outdoor living and transformation.

**Consistency at scale.** A flexible system that adapts across Clients, Contractors and Partners without fragmenting.

**Distinctiveness.** Assets that are ours, so a layout reads as Yardzen before anyone finds the logo.

